[SIZE=6][B]MC Data Bridge - Release Notes (v2.2.1)[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]Overview[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Version 2.2.1 is a release streamlining map synchronization architecture, introducing configurable map locking enforcement, fixing map canvas color palette rendering issues, and adding automatic config migration from v2.2.0.[/SIZE]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Key Changes[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]🗺️ Map Sync Architecture Simplification (#36, #39)[/B][/SIZE]

[QUOTE][B]Developer Note:[/B] [I]"I couldn't think of a single valid use case for return mode with held map items. It seemed like a good idea at first, but having a broken, unusable map item on another server would likely never be the server admin's intention."[/I][/QUOTE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Streamlined Map Synchronization Model:[/B] Removed legacy [CODE]maps.mode[/CODE] ([CODE]return[/CODE]/[CODE]untracked[/CODE] per-server stashing). Map synchronization is now toggled cleanly via [CODE]sync-data.maps: false[/CODE] (default, vanilla style handling) or [CODE]sync-data.maps: true[/CODE] (global map sync).
[*][B]Configurable Map Locking ([CODE]maps.lock-global-maps[/CODE]):[/B] Added [CODE]maps.lock-global-maps: false[/CODE] (default). When set to [CODE]true[/CODE], enforces map locking ([CODE]locked = 1[/CODE]) on cross-server maps to prevent target servers from re-scanning terrain or applying Fog of War over custom artwork.
[*][B]Automatic Legacy Config Migration:[/B] Existing [CODE]v2.2.0[/CODE] configuration files are automatically upgraded on startup:
  [LIST]
  [*]Legacy [CODE]maps.mode: global[/CODE] -> Migrated to [CODE]sync-data.maps: true[/CODE], [CODE]maps.lock-global-maps: true[/CODE].
  [*]Legacy [CODE]maps.mode: return[/CODE] / [CODE]untracked[/CODE] / [CODE]off[/CODE] -> Migrated to [CODE]sync-data.maps: false[/CODE], [CODE]maps.lock-global-maps: false[/CODE].
  [*]Obsolete [CODE]maps.mode[/CODE] config entries are automatically removed.
  [/LIST]
[*][B]Fixed [CODE]maps_nbt[/CODE] Persistence:[/B] Corrected snapshot extraction and database merge logic to ensure map snapshots and canvas pixels are saved non-null to the [CODE]{table-prefix}databridge_maps[/CODE] table.
[*][B]Locked Map Resolution Support:[/B] Improved map ID resolution logic ([CODE]resolveMapId[/CODE]) to resolve map IDs from item components and PDC ([CODE]databridge:original_map_id[/CODE]), preventing locked maps created in Cartography Tables from being skipped during saves.
[*][B]Canvas Palette & Renderer Fix:[/B] Resolved canvas rendering issues where maps rendered as solid brown blocks. Default background world renderers are now cleared ([CODE]view.getRenderers().clear()[/CODE]) before applying custom raw canvas palette byte renderers.
[/LIST]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]
[I]For installation instructions and configuration details, please refer to the README.md and config.yml.[/I]
